/bin/

# Agent tooling. .claude/skills/ is tracked deliberately: it is how a fresh
# container picks up this project's spec-driven workflow without re-running
# extension setup, which is the delegation model this project targets. The
# skill files are relative symlinks into .specify/extensions/, which is also
# tracked, so a clone resolves them.
#
# Only genuinely machine-local agent state is ignored.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Pinned tooling installed by `task tools`.
bin/

# The CRD manifests `task image` copies into the demo's kodata, out of the
# module cache, so that ko puts them in the image. Generated from the pinned
# modules at build time: committing them would be a second copy of somebody
# else's manifests, free to disagree with the code they are published for.
cmd/demo/kodata/

# Local multi-module development against the Cluster API fork.
# The pin in go.mod is the source of truth for CI and for reproduction; a
# committed go.work would silently override it for everyone.
go.work
go.work.sum

# `task demo` keeps its kcp server's state and log here, and
# `task demo:kubernetes` writes the deployed shard's kubeconfig into it. Both
# hold credentials.
.demo/

# Documentation site build output. `npm install` and `npm run build` under
# docs/site are what the documentation policy tells contributors to run, and
# they leave all of this behind; CI builds the site from a clean checkout.
docs/site/node_modules/
docs/site/public/
docs/site/resources/
docs/site/.hugo_build.lock
